<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84466" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολίζω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόλισσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.178
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλισσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.453
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις</span>):— <i>build a
				city</i>: generally, <i>build,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[τεῖχος] πολίσσαμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἣν ἐπόλισσεν</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν πάτρην</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				982
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Philae</span>):—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴλιος πεπόλιστο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.217
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δωδώνη πεπόλισται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					134.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.108
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.52
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ ἁμαξῶν πεπολισμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					6.25
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>build for oneself,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1346
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν Ῥώμην σὺν τοῖς ἄλλοις
					ἐπολίσαντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.30
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>build a city</i> or <i>cities on</i> or <i>in</i> a place, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρίον πολίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					6.6.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν χώραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					8.5.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν τόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Rom.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴη ἡ Παιονίη ἐπὶ τῷ Στρυμόνι
					ποταμῷ πεπολισμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.13
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			, 
				Ion.
			, <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i>, and later Prose.</div>
